94 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411152 1077 "field-2" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411152 1078 #edb/ref 17592186411119 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411152 1079 #uuid "e8a11ceb-0331-5fd8-8ff6-71671af48cf0" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411124 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411127 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411132 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411142 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186411143 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1077 "selection" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1078 #edb/ref 17592186411127 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411153 1079 #uuid "fbcd1085-7f9a-5980-ac51-cc2a3484d383" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411148 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1069 "q-107221" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1071 "$$\n¬(Y∧X)⇔Y≡[¬(Y∧X)⇒Y]∧\n$$\n\nWhat expression should be inserted into the blank space above to give logically equivalent statements?" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1072 #uuid "22a767fa-9117-5005-b0eb-ffcf7c23df74" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411154 1074 "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $A⇔B$ is true if $A⇒B$ **and** $B⇒A.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $A⇔B$ is true if $A$ and $B$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n¬(Y∧X)⇔Y≡[¬(Y∧X)⇒Y]∧[\\,Y⇒¬(Y∧X)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is $Y⇒¬(Y∧X).$" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411151 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1069 "q-107158" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1071 "$¬A⇔B≡$" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1072 #uuid "75186b51-1b0d-58e4-a5b9-b90965af20bd" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411155 1074 "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬A⇔B≡(¬A⇒B)∧(B⇒¬A)\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n(¬A⇒B)∧(B⇒¬A)≡(¬¬A∨B)∧(¬B∨¬A)\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n(¬¬A∨B)∧(¬B∨¬A)≡(¬¬A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n(¬¬A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)≡(A∨B)∧¬(B∧A)\n$$" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411146 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411149 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411150 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411152 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1069 "q-182580" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1072 #uuid "7dce07e5-2c84-5040-bb81-50a03090839e" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411156 1074 "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P⇔Q$ is true if $P⇒Q$ **and** $Q⇒P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P⇔Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add a columns for $X∨Y$ and $¬(X∨Y):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(X∨Y)⇔X.$ \n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)⇔X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411147 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1069 "q-182523" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1071 "$¬(Y⇔X)≡$" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1072 #uuid "96aebafe-ff76-58ac-a04c-e47b82d4e2a3" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true] [17592186411157 1074 "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬(Y⇔X)≡¬[(Y⇒X)∧(X⇒Y)]\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(Y⇒X)∧(X⇒Y)]≡¬[(¬Y∨X)∧(¬X∨Y)]\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬[(¬Y∨X)∧(¬X∨Y)] & ≡¬(¬Y∨X)∨¬(¬X∨Y) \\\\  & ≡(¬¬Y∧¬X)∨(¬¬X∧¬Y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬¬Y∧¬X)∨(¬¬X∧¬Y) & ≡(Y∧¬X)∨(X∧¬Y)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534127 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-03fc9076-17bb-57a9-be73-dfacce174097" 17592186411118 "answer-0623476e-866e-5f1b-abac-b1775984ebbf" 17592186411119 "answer-0833f240-185e-532a-824f-4ccd738ff6d6" 17592186411120 "answer-109311f5-5d8e-5ac6-9266-8b6d76321bc5" 17592186411121 "answer-2059d0ef-498b-554c-8e0d-85c9f988c719" 17592186411122 "answer-20f13fdc-83b9-522d-ab07-bb7bf6868007" 1759218641112